      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-02-18T14:06:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Actually, I believe this was previously discussed with other cards.</p><p><strong>Short version</strong>: You will always lose Ground Pound - timing is irrelevant.</p><p><strong>Long version</strong>: Start of turn triggers take effect, then start of turn decisions are made. In this case, the Ground Pound is destroyed at start of turn, then you decide if you want to skip the rest of your turn. I have to have a start of turn phase and Ground Pound goes away at that point.</p><p>Anyone else remember that conversation? ![](upload://dZUMDBWc2aavrmlv0dSHsoxpdx6.gif)&nbsp;Or am I just wrong? ![](upload://5c6IsiKf6Y9krcpaRZ8UYyVk8qA.gif)</p>",
