      "raw": "<p>If we look at Spiff&#39;s clarifications document we get</p><div>but what about your start-of-turn phase? in most cases, cards will say &ldquo;at the&nbsp;</div><div>start of your turn, you may skip the rest of your turn to do xyz&rdquo;. because&nbsp;</div><div>start-of-turn effects are activated in the order in which they were played, if&nbsp;</div><div>you have other cards with start-of-turn effects which were in play before the&nbsp;</div><div>card which is causing you to skip the rest of your turn, those start-of-turn&nbsp;</div><div>effects will happen first, then you&rsquo;ll skip everything else.[br]&nbsp;</div><div>[br]</div><div>And as we all know Spiff doesn&#39;t put anything in there not clarified by a voice from on high.</div><div>I&#39;m sure if we really wanted to we could find the original post so Spiff could add that to his documentation, which might be a good project for us all to contribute to.</div>",
