    {
      "id": 92348,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-02-18T23:53:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My understanding of Start Phase actions is as has been stated above - they occur in the order in which they were played. So if Omni-10 managed to put out all his components and then Mars played the Self-Destruct Sequence, at the start of his turn Omni-10 would be able to have all his components do their stuff (in the order they entered play) and <span class=\"bbcode-i\">then</span> decide if he wanted to skip his turn to add to the countdown. Even better if he has a Bio-Engineering Beam handy, of course ;).</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:18:15.909Z",
